            <div class='post' itemprop='text'>
              <p>Hey everyone,</p>
<p>Korean Developer Engagement Team (<a class="mention" href="/u/lvl100superburrito">@lvl100superburrito</a>, <a class="mention" href="/u/soobsok">@soobsok</a>, <a class="mention" href="/u/cafemochaventi">@cafemochaventi</a>, and <a class="mention" href="/u/ssamssam33">@ssamssam33</a>) here! We’ve had the pleasure of meeting some of you already, and we’re excited to share a recap of the first-ever in-person Korean Community Event, which took place on November 15-16 in Busan, South Korea!</p>
<p>Before getting into the workshops, we wanted to highlight some of the activities that went on during the event! Creators had the chance to do deep dive sessions and get feedback from <a class="mention" href="/u/six5creedmore">@Six5Creedmore</a>, Senior Game Producer. There was also a claw machine where people could draw prizes after completing challenges, a gameplay area, an interactive wall, and a cute photo booth to take pictures from! Attendees also received the exclusive <a href="https://www.roblox.com/catalog/137490420774313/Developer-Dragon">Developer Dragon</a> virtual item!</p>
<div align="center">
<p><div class="lightbox-wrapper"><a class="lightbox" href="//devforum-uploads.s3.dualstack.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/uploads/original/5X/f/c/2/1/fc217facc36656cac228c7744ed905ab37e519c7.jpeg" data-download-href="/uploads/short-url/zYs5MsjV3z4W2J6fN3pUCrCerdB.jpeg?dl=1" title="Intro"><img src="//devforum-uploads.s3.dualstack.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/uploads/optimized/5X/f/c/2/1/fc217facc36656cac228c7744ed905ab37e519c7_2_690x138.jpeg" alt="Intro" data-base62-sha1="7TW5MBY4ExtDHUgkIDPfTYH1tl1" width="690" height="138" srcset="//devforum-uploads.s3.dualstack.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/uploads/optimized/5X/f/c/2/1/fc217facc36656cac228c7744ed905ab37e519c7_2_690x138.jpeg, //devforum-uploads.s3.dualstack.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/uploads/optimized/5X/f/c/2/1/fc217facc36656cac228c7744ed905ab37e519c7_2_1035x207.jpeg 1.5x, //devforum-uploads.s3.dualstack.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/uploads/optimized/5X/f/c/2/1/fc217facc36656cac228c7744ed905ab37e519c7_2_1380x276.jpeg 2x" data-dominant-color="8A8991"><div class="meta">
<svg class="fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#far-image"></use></svg><span class="filename">Intro</span><span class="informations">1920×386 54.5 KB</span><svg class="fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#discourse-expand"></use></svg>
</div></a></div></p>
<div align="left">
<p>Here’s a summary of the workshops, some of which were hosted by our community.</p>
<details>
<summary>
Rift Hunters - Brave Turtles x Jeny Punker Collaboration</summary>
<p>The collaboration between BraveTurtles X Jeny Punker allows influencers and developers to connect and work together. To achieve success through collaboration, we need to ensure we have specific goals and roles and to respect each other’s styles and perspectives. Some strategies for collaboration include giving feedback, creating a timeline, and creating a roadmap together to make the story, animate content, and understand the experience. While reviewing the success of the collaboration on social media, take the opportunity to gather any user feedback you come across. In conclusion, communicating openly, understanding each other, finding what works best for both parties and playing the game by ourselves to understand specific details and highlighting them are important in working together.</p>
